<section class="bhd-page__feature"><div><p class="bhd-page__kicker">Partnership principle</p><h2>Start with the outcome, then design the relationship</h2><p>A partnership is useful when both sides can explain what success means. Research partners may need a protocol and publication plan. Retail partners need a product and customer fit. Humanitarian partners need local context, logistics, safe-water infrastructure and a way to measure whether the intervention actually works.</p><p>Best Hydrate does not treat those as the same conversation, and the pages below are intentionally separated for that reason.</p></div></section>

<section class="bhd-page__cards-section"><p class="bhd-page__kicker">Choose a path</p><h2>Three ways to collaborate</h2><div class="bhd-page__cards bhd-page__cards--3">
  <article><h3>Research Partnerships</h3><p>Collaborate on hydration questions, study methods, product evaluation, pilots or knowledge translation with clear evidence standards.</p><a href="/pages/research-partnerships">Research Partnerships →</a></article>
  <article><h3>Retail & Distribution</h3><p>Explore channel fit, merchandising, education and regional growth without requiring exaggerated product claims.</p><a href="/pages/retail-distribution">Retail & Distribution →</a></article>
  <article><h3>Humanitarian Partnerships</h3><p>Develop access projects with local implementation, safe-water requirements and appropriate therapeutic standards in view.</p><a href="/pages/humanitarian-partnerships">Humanitarian Partnerships →</a></article>
</div></section>

<section class="bhd-page__split"><div class="bhd-page__split-media"><img src="https://images.pexels.com/photos/4031524/pexels-photo-4031524.jpeg?auto=compress&cs=tinysrgb&w=1500" alt="Two researchers reviewing information together in a laboratory" width="1500" height="1000" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></div><div class="bhd-page__split-copy"><p class="bhd-page__kicker">What good partners share</p><h2>Clear roles, useful feedback and willingness to test assumptions</h2><p>Best Hydrate is still building. The most valuable partners are not simply logos beside the brand. They bring a customer, scientific, operational or local perspective that can improve the product, the evidence or the way a project is implemented.</p><p>That also means being comfortable with iteration. A pilot may reveal that the initial plan should change. A retailer may identify a better customer segment. A research collaborator may narrow a claim. Those are productive outcomes when the goal is long-term credibility.</p></div></section>

<section class="bhd-page__cards-section"><p class="bhd-page__kicker">A simple working sequence</p><h2>From first conversation to useful work</h2><div class="bhd-page__cards bhd-page__cards--4"><article><h3>1. Fit</h3><p>Define the problem, audience and why Best Hydrate is relevant.</p></article><article><h3>2. Scope</h3><p>Agree on roles, deliverables, evidence requirements, commercial terms or implementation boundaries.</p></article><article><h3>3. Pilot</h3><p>Start at a scale that can produce useful learning before expanding.</p></article><article><h3>4. Review</h3><p>Assess results, document lessons and decide whether to continue, change or stop.</p></article></div></section>

<section class="bhd-page__brand-context"><div><p class="bhd-page__kicker">Start the conversation</p><h2>Tell us what you are trying to accomplish</h2><p>A useful first message includes your organization, the problem you are working on, the population or market involved, and what you think Best Hydrate could contribute.</p></div><div class="bhd-page__brand-actions"><a class="bhd-page__button" href="/pages/contact">Contact Best Hydrate</a><a class="bhd-page__button bhd-page__button--secondary" href="/pages/mission-values">Mission & Values</a></div></section>

